Related event seed (flyers, not album): [`scripts/seed-mcefee-events-from-charity-site.mjs`](mdc:scripts/seed-mcefee-events-from-charity-site.mjs).

### Typical commands

```bash
# Create/upload album (Next must be up for proxy upload path)
node scripts/seed-mcefee-gallery-album.mjs --app-url http://localhost:3002

# Relink media if upload left albumId null
node scripts/seed-mcefee-gallery-album.mjs --link-only

# Preview keep/delete (OCR)
node scripts/filter-mcefee-gallery-album.mjs --dry-run

# Apply filter: keep mcefee (filename/OCR) + exec team; delete rest
node scripts/filter-mcefee-gallery-album.mjs --album-id 64
```

Requires `.env.local`: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_ID`, `API_JWT_USER` / `API_JWT_PASS`.

## Upload Pattern

1. **Authenticate** with service JWT (`getServiceJwt` from gallery-porting-lib).
2. **Create album** via `POST /api/gallery-albums` (optional `galleryCategoryId`; category seed may fail on DB sequence — album can ship with `galleryCategoryId=null`).
3. **Upload** via Next proxy `POST {appUrl}/api/proxy/event-medias/upload-multiple` **or** backend `POST /api/event-medias/upload?...&albumId=...` with `Authorization` + `X-Tenant-ID`.
4. **Always PATCH** media after upload — multipart upload often leaves `albumId=null`:

```javascript
// merge-patch with full required non-null fields (see seed script patchAlbumId)
PATCH /api/event-medias/{id}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
{ id, albumId, fileUrl, title, tenantId, eventMediaType, storageType, createdAt, updatedAt, ... }
```

5. **Cover image**: `PATCH /api/gallery-albums/{albumId}` with `coverImageUrl` set to the chosen media’s `fileUrl` (e.g. `mcefee_logo_black_border_transparent.png`).

## OCR / Image Scraping for Keep-Set

**Goal:** Decide keep vs delete from **what the image shows**, not from seed metadata alone.

### DO

- Prefer **local file OCR** when the same filename exists under charity-site / `public/images/**` (S3 download may fail without public access).
- Use **Tesseract** (installed path often `C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe`; override with `TESSERACT_PATH`).
- Match brand text with a regex on OCR stdout **and** on whitespace-collapsed text (logos OCR as `M CE FE E` / `KCNJ.ORG`).
- Match **filename/title only** for text heuristics (e.g. `/mcefee/i` on `title` / URL basename).
- Optionally use sibling project **`F:\project_workspace\image-edit-ai-tools`** Gemini describe (`/api/nano-banana`, `action: 'describe'`) when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is available — same “read the image” idea as OCR.

### DON’T

- ❌ Use **description** / seed alt text for “contains mcefee” — seed scripts often write `KCNJ modernist: …` on every file and will false-keep everything.
- ❌ Treat modernist placeholders `team_1.jpg`…`team_4.jpg` as executive committee — keep only real roster photos (`profileImageUrl` / names like `shaji_varghese.jpeg`).
- ❌ Trust a single noisy OCR hit without a dry-run; re-check borderline keeps (collapsed OCR can false-positive).

### Keep rules used for Mcefee Album

1. Filename/title contains `mcefee`, **or**
2. OCR finds `mcefee` / `KCNJ` (incl. email/domain), **or**
3. Image is an **executive-committee** member photo (`/api/executive-committee-team-members` → field **`profileImageUrl`**, not `imageUrl`).

Delete non-matches with `DELETE /api/event-medias/{id}`.

## Executive Committee Images

- Admin UI: `/admin/executive-committee`.
- API: `GET /api/executive-committee-team-members?tenantId.equals=...`.
- Image field: **`profileImageUrl`**.
- If those URLs are not already `event_medias` rows in the album, **upload** local files from  
  `NJ-Malayalees-MCEEFEE-Charity-Site/images/team_members/` and PATCH `albumId` (see filter script).

## Anti-Patterns

```javascript
// ❌ DON'T: keep if description mentions brand (seed pollution)
const keep = /mcefee/i.test(media.description);

// ✅ DO: filename + OCR on pixels
const keep = /mcefee/i.test(media.title) || ocrTextHasMcefee(localOrDownloadedPath);

// ❌ DON'T: assume upload bound the album
await upload(...); // albumId may still be null

// ✅ DO: PATCH albumId after every upload
await patchAlbumId(token, media, albumId, displayOrder);
```

